# 9. Relationship of the Original Retrieval Path to Current TenantSage

The TenantSage Real-Time Inheritance Retrieval Path™ remains technically present.

The original mechanism contained:

```text
Parent-source governance
+
mandatory source inheritance
+
scope enforcement
+
role / visibility enforcement
+
temporal validity
+
legal-hold enforcement
+
whitelist-controlled precedence
+
vector ranking after governance
```

That mechanism is now positioned inside the larger architecture.

Current canonical placement:

```text
S0 Request Ingress

        ↓

S1 Deterministic Authority Resolution

        ↓

S2 Governance Decision

        ↓

S3 Sealed Eligible Evidence Boundary

        ↓

S4 TrustRAG
   Real-Time Inheritance Retrieval
   Ghost Effect
   Parent-Source Governance

        ↓

S5 Governed Context

        ↓

S6 Generation

        ↓

S7 Validation

        ↓

S8 Approval-Bound Execution
   where external action is required
```

The earlier architecture has therefore **not been discarded**.

Its technical mechanism remains present as the retrieval enforcement foundation.

Current TenantSage adds:

### Before retrieval

* explicit identity verification;
* deterministic authority resolution;
* active scope;
* governance state;
* sealed evidence eligibility.

### After retrieval

* governed context;
* controlled generation;
* validation;
* explicit execution approval;
* exact-material binding;
* durable intent proof;
* outcome verification;
* durable completion proof;
* replay evidence.

This creates an end-to-end governance chain rather than a retrieval-only governance mechanism.

